# npl-rubric - reference-page UX direction for the five display states.
# Authored by the tag nitpick lane, 2026-10-14. Not yet generated.
schema: "0.4"
id: npl-rubric-reference-ux
type: image
quality: high
prompt:
  text: |
    Design board for a reference-documentation page, dark theme (deep
    navy-charcoal surfaces, near-white text, muted slate secondary text,
    a single indigo-blue accent). The page documents a weighted scoring
    rubric element: one small table of criteria, each row naming a
    criterion with a numeric weight and a numeric score, closed by an
    "Overall" footer row carrying a single figure. The board shows FIVE
    stacked example sections, one per display state, each with a small
    uppercase caption above it. No marketing chrome, no navigation, no
    browser window - five quiet document panels on a flat dark page.

    Every panel is the same card: a faint surface fill, a hairline border,
    a 12px radius, generous but regular padding; inside sits a compact
    two-to-three column table. Column heads are small, uppercase, widely
    letter-spaced, muted: "CRITERION" left-aligned, "WEIGHT" and "SCORE"
    right-aligned. Numeric cells use tabular monospace figures aligned in a
    clean right column. Row labels are a neutral sans at full brightness. A
    hairline rule separates the column heads from the rows and the rows from
    the footer.

    Section 1 - "STATED OVERALL": caption line "Code review", two rows
    (Correctness 3 4, Style 1 5), then the footer row "Overall (STATED)"
    with the figure 4.2 right-aligned. The footer row carries a thin
    indigo-blue accent bar on its left edge and a barely-there accent tint
    (about 12% opacity, never an opaque block) across the row; the word
    Overall is semibold and the qualifier "(STATED)" is small-caps muted.
    The figure itself is monospace, bold-ish, right-aligned.

    Section 2 - "COMPUTED OVERALL": caption "Deployment readiness", three
    rows (Rollback plan 2 5, Alerting 1 4, Runbook 1 5), footer
    "Overall (COMPUTED) 4.75". The row MUST carry the parenthetical marker
    "(COMPUTED)" in the same small-caps muted style as section 1 - a bare
    figure with no stated/computed marker is a failure.

    Section 3 - "EXCLUDED CRITERIA": caption "Triage", four rows. Impact 2 4
    is ordinary. Confidence has its weight cell as an em dash and the score
    5; Urgency has weight "high" and score 3; Cost has weight 1 and an em
    dash score. Under each of those three names sits a small second line in
    the warning red-tint - "ignored - no numeric weight" for the first two,
    "ignored - no numeric score" for the last. Those three rows are QUIETED
    only in the sense that the dash cells and the flag line are muted/red;
    their names, weights and scores stay at full brightness and fully
    legible - an excluded row is marked and kept, never hidden, dimmed to
    illegibility, or struck through. Footer "Overall (COMPUTED) 4".

    Section 4 - "CLASS-FORM (DATA-TITLE)": caption "Class-form rubric", two
    rows (Correctness 3 4, Clarity 1 5), footer "Overall (STATED) 4.25".
    Rendered identically to section 1 - the board shows the result, not the
    authoring form.

    Section 5 - "OVERALL WITHOUT CRITERIA": caption "Sign-off", the column
    heads present, NO criterion rows, and the footer "Overall (STATED) 4.6"
    directly under the head rule - a rubric that is only a title and a
    figure still reads as a complete small table, with no empty box, no
    placeholder row, no "0" or "n/a" filler.

    Typography: monospace for figures, the em dashes and the mode captions;
    a clean neutral sans for criterion names and the word Overall. Hairline
    borders, small radii, spacing tight and regular. Everything must read as
    quiet instrumentation inside a spec document, not as a dashboard widget.
  negative: |
    Light theme; white background; glossy gradients; neon cyberpunk glow;
    dashboard card grids; donut, pie, gauge, radar, sparkline or bar charts;
    progress bars; star ratings; checkmarks or crosses as scores; sliders;
    mascots; logos; watermarks; navigation bars; browser chrome; more or
    fewer than five named sections; a section with no caption; an overall
    figure without its (STATED)/(COMPUTED) marker; a fully opaque accent
    block as the footer row; hidden, struck-through, greyed-out or legible-
    defeated excluded rows; an em-dash row rendered as zero; modal dialogs
    or toast popups; any imagery other than the five tables.
  style: |
    Flat minimal dark technical documentation, minimal-tech aesthetic,
    table-first restraint, hairline rules, monospace numerals, WCAG AA
    contrast on all text including the warning-tinted flag lines.
attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-rubric/npl-rubric-render-stated-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-rubric/npl-rubric-render-computed-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-rubric/npl-rubric-render-excluded-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-rubric/npl-rubric-render-class-form-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-rubric/npl-rubric-render-overall-only-390.png
    role: reference
output:
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: npl-rubric-reference-ux.png
eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  criteria:
    state-coverage:
      weight: 0.3
      description: Exactly five captioned sections in order - stated, computed, excluded, class-form, overall-without-criteria; overall-only has no criterion rows.
      fail_signals:
        - "only one or two sections visible"
        - "sections unlabelled or mislabelled"
        - "the overall-without-criteria section shows filler rows"
    table-anatomy:
      weight: 0.3
      description: Every section is a real table - CRITERION/WEIGHT/SCORE heads, right-aligned tabular figures, hairline rules, and an Overall footer row with a (STATED)/(COMPUTED) marker.
      fail_signals:
        - "column heads missing"
        - "figures not right-aligned or not tabular"
        - "overall figure with no stated/computed marker"
    exclusion-legibility:
      weight: 0.25
      description: Excluded rows keep full-brightness names and values, show an em dash for the missing cell, and carry a warning-tinted "ignored - <reason>" line; footer averages only the included criteria.
      fail_signals:
        - "excluded row dimmed, struck through or hidden"
        - "missing cell rendered as 0 rather than an em dash"
        - "no reason line under an excluded criterion"
    theme-match:
      weight: 0.15
      description: Dark minimal-tech surfaces, hairline borders, mono/sans split, AA-legible text including the red-tinted flags, footer tint restrained to a light accent wash.
      fail_signals:
        - "light background anywhere"
        - "neon glow or gradient gloss"
        - "solid opaque accent block as the footer"
  reject_if:
    - "image is light-themed overall"
    - "any chart, gauge or dashboard widget replaces the tables"
    - "fewer than five captioned sections"
tags:
  - semtext
  - npl-rubric
  - reference-design
  - dark-ui